{"qid":"Q211","names":["Republic of Latvia"],"title":"Republic of Latvia","endonym":{"native":"Latvija","lang":"lv"},"capsule":"The Republic of Latvia declared independence on 18 November 1918 following the collapse of the Russian Empire, and secured its borders through the Treaty of Riga with Soviet Russia on 11 August 1920. The interwar republic developed a parliamentary democracy that was replaced in 1934 by the authoritarian government of Kārlis Ulmanis; the Soviet occupation of 1940, followed by German occupation 1941–1944 and renewed Soviet annexation, extinguished the state until the Supreme Soviet of the Latvian SSR declared the restoration of independence on 4 May 1990, internationally recognized after the August 1991 coup. Latvia joined NATO and the European Union in 2004 and adopted the euro in 2014.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Latvia's borders with Estonia, Lithuania, Russia, and Belarus are clearly delimited by successive treaties; the 1920 start date reflects the peace treaty with Soviet Russia rather than the 1918 declaration.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Latvia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latvia"},{"label":"Britannica: Latvia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Latvia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Treaty of Riga (1920)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Riga_(1920)"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Kārlis Ulmanis","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K%C4%81rlis_Ulmanis"}],"britannica":"place/Latvia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Latvia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q379554","name":"Jānis Čakste","start":1922,"end":1927,"image":"Janis Cakste.jpg","imageUrl":"https://c